## claude --version: 2.1.328 (Claude Code)
## claude --help, the option lines for --resume, --model, --fork-session and --name, three lines after each
  --fork-session                        When resuming, create a new session ID
                                        instead of reusing the original (use
                                        with --resume or --continue)
  --forward-subagent-text               Forward subagent text and thinking
--
  --model <model>                       Model for the current session. Use an
                                        alias for the latest model (e.g.
                                        'fable', 'opus', or 'sonnet') or a
                                        model's full name.
  -n, --name <name>                     Set a display name for this session
                                        (shown in the prompt box, /resume
                                        picker, and terminal title)
  --no-chrome                           Turn off Claude in Chrome
--
  -r, --resume [value]                  Resume a conversation by session ID or
                                        name, or pick from a list (optionally
                                        with a search term)
  --safe-mode                           Start with all customizations
## codex resume --help (first 40 lines)
## codex --version: codex-cli 0.169.0
Resume a previous interactive session (picker by default; use --last to continue the most recent)

Usage: codex resume [OPTIONS] [SESSION_ID] [PROMPT]

Arguments:
  [SESSION_ID]
          Session id (UUID) or session name. UUIDs take precedence if it parses. If omitted, use
          --last to pick the most recent recorded session

  [PROMPT]
          Optional user prompt to start the session

Options:
  -c, --config <key=value>
          Override a configuration value that would otherwise be loaded from `~/.codex/config.toml`.
          Use a dotted path (`foo.bar.baz`) to override nested values. The `value` portion is parsed
          as TOML. If it fails to parse as TOML, the raw string is used as a literal.
          
          Examples: - `-c model="o3"` - `-c 'sandbox_permissions=["disk-full-read-access"]'` - `-c
          shell_environment_policy.inherit=all`

      --last
          Continue the most recent session without showing the picker

      --all
          Show all sessions (disables cwd filtering and shows CWD column)

      --enable <FEATURE>
          Enable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=true`

      --disable <FEATURE>
          Disable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=false`

      --include-non-interactive
          Include non-interactive sessions in the resume picker and --last selection

      --remote <ADDR>
          Connect the TUI to a remote app server endpoint.
          
          Accepted forms: `ws://host:port`, `wss://host:port`, `unix://`, or `unix://PATH`.
## agy --help | grep -iE 'conversation|resume|model|continue'
## agy --version: 1.5.9
  -c                              Short alias for --continue
  --continue                      Continue the most recent conversation
  --conversation                  Resume a previous conversation by ID
  --model                         Model for the current CLI session
  --prompt-interactive            Run an initial prompt interactively and continue the session
  --remote-agent                  Run this session's conversations using remote agents; --project then names a remote project by ID or name, otherwise they open in this machine's default remote project
  models          List available models
## handoff settings claude --global: the hooks that run handoff hook listen
  Notification: handoff hook notify
  SessionStart: handoff hook brief, handoff hook listen (asyncRewake)
  Stop: handoff hook listen (asyncRewake)
## handoff settings codex --global: the hooks
  SessionStart: exec handoff hook brief
  Stop: exec handoff hook listen
# so a resumed Claude Code session listens from its start; a resumed Codex session listens once a turn ends (Antigravity likewise: antigravity's Stop hook, row 102)
